UID:8c1ffa17e147@paris-academique
DTSTAMP:20260521T142943Z
DTSTART:20260521T140000
DTEND:20260521T150000
SUMMARY:Binary Boson stars in Strong Field: Post-Minkowskian\, Effective-one-body formalism\, and Numerical Relativity
DESCRIPTION:In this talk\, I will present our recent work on scattering of two boson stars by taking into account three effects: point-mass gravitational\, tidal\, and short-range scalar-field interactions. We first derive the analytical expressions of the scattering angle using PM-EFT techniques\, providing the first analytical treatment of boson stars as a two-body problem. We then compare analytic results to t\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16434/
LOCATION:Salle des séminaires
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16434/
END:VEVENT
