SUMMARY:On the generating series of degree sequences in algebraic dynamics
DESCRIPTION:In algebraic dynamics\, dynamical degrees are fundamental birational invariants that capture the growth of degree sequences. In 2020\, Bell\, Diller\, and Jonsson gave the first example of a rational map whose dynamical degree is transcendental by studying the generating series of its degree sequences. In this talk\, I will present some analytic and algebraic properties of such series for monomial maps\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16161/
