SUMMARY:Origami and algebra
DESCRIPTION:In an origami construction\, we start with an infinite sheet of paper that we can consider to be the complex plane\, with two marked points on it: 0 and 1. Origami constructions consist simply of a series of folds in the paper following certain axiomatic rules\, using pre-existing points and lines. When the paper is folded and unfolded\, it leaves a crease which is an affine line. In our setting\, a po\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16345/
