SUMMARY:The Refined Toledo Invariant of a Non-Archimedean Surface Group Representation
DESCRIPTION:Let S be a compact oriented surface with boundary\, Γ its fundamental group\, and G a simple algebraic group defined over Q such that the symmetric space associated to G ( R ) is Hermitian of tube type. Given a real closed field F and a canonical presentation of Γ \, we define for a representation of Γ in G ( F ) an invariant taking values in an ordered abelian group A ( F )\, called the refined Toled\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16444/
